CODEx TASK: Reduce Docker build context size by adding a strict .dockerignore.

Context:
- Current Docker build transfers ~5GB context (slow startup).
- This repo is an RNA-seq pipeline where runtime data/refs are provided via volume mounts (/input, /output). Therefore large datasets and run outputs must NOT be part of the build context.

Requirements:
1) Add a .dockerignore at the repository root.
2) Exclude:
   - pipeline outputs, caches, logs, Snakemake working dirs
   - sequencing data and common bioinformatics bulky artifacts (fastq/bam/etc.)
   - Python/Node cache dirs
   - Git metadata and OS junk
3) Keep source code, Dockerfile(s), workflow/ scripts/ app/ tests/ configs, and docs included.
4) After adding, verify build context shrinks substantially by running:
   - docker build --no-cache -t harako-rnaseq:dev .
   - Confirm the “transferring context” size is small (MB order, not GB).

Deliverable:
- Commit the .dockerignore with message like: "chore(docker): add .dockerignore to shrink build context"

Create file: .dockerignore (repo root)
------------------------------------------------
# --- VCS / editor / OS ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*.tmp

# --- Python caches ---
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/.tox/
**/.nox/

# --- Node / frontend caches (if any) ---
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.nuxt/
**/dist/
**/build/

# --- Snakemake / workflow runtime state ---
**/.snakemake/
**/snakemake_logs/
**/logs/
**/log/
**/*.log

# --- Harako / pipeline outputs & caches (common names) ---
output/
out/
data_out/
results/
report/
reports/
refs_cache/
ref_cache/
.cache/
tmp/
temp/

# --- Large bioinformatics / sequencing data (MUST NOT be in build context) ---
**/*.fastq
**/*.fq
**/*.fastq.gz
**/*.fq.gz
**/*.bam
**/*.bam.bai
**/*.sam
**/*.cram
**/*.crai
**/*.sra
**/*.gtf
**/*.gtf.gz
**/*.gff
**/*.gff.gz
**/*.fa
**/*.fasta
**/*.fa.gz
**/*.fasta.gz
**/*.fna
**/*.fna.gz
**/*.bed
**/*.bed.gz

# --- Optional: raw imaging / bulky scientific formats (safety) ---
**/*.tif
**/*.tiff
**/*.nd2
**/*.h5
**/*.hdf5

# --- Optional: archives / huge misc ---
**/*.zip
**/*.tar
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.tgz
**/*.7z